  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Examine the four expressions below. Which one doesn't belong?</para>
    
    <para>\((x + 4)(x − 3)\)</para>
    <para>\(3x^2 − 8x + 5\)</para>
    <para>\(x^2 − 25\)</para>
    <para>\(x^2 + 2x + 3\)</para>
    <para>There are many possible answers for which equation does not belong in a group with the others. Determine which equation you think should be eliminated and explain your reasoning.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your explanation.</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para> Equation A: The only expression that is not in standard form. Or, when written in standard form, it is the only one that has an even number for the constant term.</para>
    
    <para>Equation B: The only expression in standard form that has a leading coefficient other than 1.</para>
    
    <para>Equation C: The only expression in standard form that doesn't have three terms. It is the only one without a linear term.</para>
    
    <para>Equation D: The only expression in standard form that can't be written in factored form. It is prime.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise></section>
</content>
